# Slice 334 (the author 2026-11-09: `name: "test"` with an existing callable name obeys the ordinary call of that
# callable): with the function name declared, the Frame `name: 7` is the call name(7), applied once where the traversal
# reaches the receiver's Frame; its value binds no part name, and the receiver is refused (the interpreter answers 5;
# native and forced code fail there).
fn: name (int: x) int (int: calls 0)
    calls := calls + 1
    return: x
end: name
int: r1 1
fn: name: 7; args: (int: a); return: int; body: (return: a)
int: r2 2
